  "solution": {
    "text": "When the particle is in its mean position, the kinetic energy will be maximum,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>K</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mtext>m</mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mtext>a</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>5.12</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mtext>T</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mtext>0.25</mtext></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mtext>T</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>2.56</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>0.25</mtext></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>0.25</mtext></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>T</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>1.6</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>0.25</mtext></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
